	? "Whats the main advantage of dome cameras?" -> Difficult to determine direction; tamper-resistant

$ Locks
	- Purpose: Locks restrict physical access to sensitive areas like server rooms, network closets, and data racks - preventing unauthorized users from physically compromising the network
	- Common Lock Types:
		Lock Type         | Description                                                                           | Use Case
		Keyed Locks       | Traditional lock-and-key mechanisms. Low cost, but easily duplicated or picked        | Office doors, basic protection
		Combination Locks | Require a numeric code. No key duplication risk                                       | Shared spaces, small enclosures
		Electronic Locks  | Use keypads, proximity cards, or RFID tags. Often connected to access control systems | Data centers, network rooms
		Smart Locks       | Controlled via network or Bluetooth; logs access events                               | High-security environments or smart offices
		Biometric Locks   | Use fingerprints, facial recognition, or retina scans                                 | Server racks, high-security facilities
		Cable Locks       | Metal cables looped through laptops or equipment                                      | Prevents device theft
